</source_material>

<execution_protocol>
You must execute your response in two phases:

PHASE 1: <scratchpad>
Before generating the final output, you must use a <scratchpad> block to mentally plan the script.
1. Identify the core facts from the transcript.
2. Select your Narrative Framework (A, B, C, or D).
3. Draft your Title and verify it has exactly 0 punctuation marks and is 6-10 words.
4. Draft the Hook and the Closer, ensuring they form a perfect, grammatical infinite loop.
5. Verify you have not used any quotes, dialogue, or forbidden formatting.

PHASE 2: Final Output
Following the scratchpad, provide the final output EXACTLY in this format, with no markdown code blocks surrounding it:

TITLE: [Your Title Here]
DESCRIPTION: [Your Description Here]
TAGS: [Your Tags Here]

[Your plain text script body here, starting directly with the hook]
</execution_protocol>